  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). A Chinese-language workbench where a clinical researcher loads an Excel study table, checks and cleans it, runs descriptive, inferential, predictive, survival and causal analyses, and exports chosen results as a Word, Excel or figure-pack report with an auto-drafted methods paragraph. Department quality-control staff can also use it on its own to chart indicators over time. Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
